#
# fa18.obj - F/A-18 Hornet, low-poly
#
# Geometry:   a fighter 54 feet from nose to tail and 40 across the wings,
#             about the pilot's eye: x toward the right wing, y up and z
#             toward the tail. A fuselage of four diamond sections behind a
#             pointed nose, closed, and thin plates for the wings, the
#             leading edge extensions, the stabilizers, the two tails canted
#             outward and the gear, each plate one face per side. Every face
#             winds counterclockwise seen from the side it shows.
# Materials:  jet, the body and plates; canopy, the first stretch of the
#             fuselage's top; gear, the legs, shown only when they are down.
# Components: 57 vertices, 1 UV coordinate, since the jet is untextured,
#             41 face normals, and 41 faces, 8 of them triangles and the
#             rest quads.
# Used by:    flightsim2.
#
